      "content": "I get that, but I'm looking for more of a predictive model than just standard indicators. When looking at the demographic maps, there's usually a correlation between the racial makeup of a district and its long-term market stability. In your experience analyzing these patterns, does a high level of racial diversity typically act as a signal for market volatility or declining property values compared to more homogeneous areas? I need to understand the risk profile of diversifying neighborhoods.",
